RESULTS

Competition Results

The Obstacle Course Racing Association of Ireland (OCRA ÉIREANN) aims to maintain a clear and permanent record of results from OCRA competitions, National Championships, qualification events and major international performances involving Irish athletes.

Results are an important part of the history of the sport and should remain accessible long after an individual event has finished.


Recent Results

The most recent competition results should be available directly from this page.

Results may include:

- Athlete name
- Overall position
- Category position
- Discipline
- Age Group
- Time or score
- Penalties
- Result status
- Qualification result
- Medal result


Official and Provisional Results

Immediately after a competition, results may initially be published as:

PROVISIONAL

This allows time for any corrections, protests or result reviews.

Once the relevant competition process has been completed, results may be confirmed as:

OFFICIAL


Result Classifications

Depending on the competition rules, results may include classifications such as:

DNS — Did Not Start

DNF — Did Not Finish

DNC — Did Not Complete

DSQ — Disqualified


The exact use of each classification depends on the competition rules.


National Championship Results

OCRA aims to maintain a permanent record of Irish National Championship results.

This includes recognition of:

- Irish National Champions
- Silver medallists
- Bronze medallists
- Age Group results
- Elite results
- Discipline-specific results


Qualification Results

Where an event forms part of an international qualification pathway, its results should clearly identify the qualification event and provide access to the relevant qualification information.

Athletes should refer to the current Qualification page for confirmation of qualification requirements.


Team Ireland Results

Results achieved by athletes representing Ireland at major international competition form an important part of Ireland's obstacle sport history.

OCRA aims to preserve these performances as part of the Team Ireland and Results archives.


Athlete Results

As the OCRA results archive develops, athletes should be able to view their performances across multiple competitions.

An athlete's results record may include:

- Events
- Disciplines
- Finishing positions
- Times
- Age Group results
- Medal performances
- Team Ireland appearances

This will help create a long-term competitive history for Irish obstacle racing.


Results Archive

Historical results should remain accessible by year and event.

This may include:

- OCRA competitions
- National Championships
- Qualification events
- European Championships
- World Championships
- Team Ireland results

Preserving historical results allows athletes, clubs and the wider community to follow the development of the sport over time.


Corrections

If you believe that an OCRA result has been recorded incorrectly, contact OCRA with details of:

- Event
- Athlete
- Discipline
- Category
- Result requiring review

OCRA will review correction requests against the official competition records.


